    <innerclass refid="classWatchDog" prot="public">WatchDog</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Background health monitor for the pooled database connections. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares <ref refid="classWatchDog" kindref="compound">WatchDog</ref>, a small class that owns a background thread. The thread wakes once per interval, leases one pooled connection through a <ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref>, checks whether the link is alive, and reconnects it (and the rest of the idle pool) when it is not. An atomic flag lets the destructor signal shutdown and then join the thread cleanly.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Databases restart and network links drop; without monitoring, a stalled connection would keep failing requests until somebody manually restarted the server. The watchdog runs in the background at startup and silently repairs connections, cooperating with <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1a51134b38454f5146921c081fbf2ad5f3" kindref="member">DatabaseConnectionPool::reconnect_all()</ref>. It is the self-healing part of the synchronous database path: controllers do not need to know that a link died and came back.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>std::thread (a real background thread of execution): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::atomic (a flag readable/writable from two threads without races): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>join() (wait for a thread to finish before destroying its owner): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread/join">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread/join</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>RAII (the destructor stops and joins the thread): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::chrono::seconds (a time duration): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/duration">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/duration</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
